            <ArticleTitle>Cerebral venous sinus thrombosis in HIV-infected patients: report of 2 cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11604/pamj.2013.16.4.3252</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Infection with the human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is associated with increased risk of cerebrovascular disease; however Cerebral Venous Sinus Thrombosis (CVST) is rarely associated with HIV-related cerebrovascular events. We describe two cases of HIV-positive patients who, at the same time, presented to our hospital with deep cerebral venous thrombosis and stroke.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
